  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A\u2261\\text{T}$ and $C\u2261\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acC\u2227(A\u2228C) & \u2261\u00ac\\text{T}\u2227(\\text{T}\u2228\\text{T}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2227\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A\u2261\\text{T}$ and $C\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acC\u2227(A\u2228C) & \u2261\u00ac\\text{F}\u2227(\\text{T}\u2228\\text{F}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2227\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A\u2261\\text{F}$ and $C\u2261\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(\u00acA\u2227\u00acC)\u2227\u00acC & \u2261\u00ac(\u00ac\\text{F}\u2227\u00ac\\text{T})\u2227\u00ac\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2227\\text{F})\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac\\text{F}\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,C\\,$ | $\\,\u00ac(\u00acA\u2227\u00acC)\u2227\u00acC\\,$ | $\\,\u00acC\u2227(A\u2228C)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $\u00ac(\u00acA\u2227\u00acC)\u2227\u00acC$ is logically equivalent to $\u00acC\u2227(A\u2228C),$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.  \n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00acA\u2227\u00acC)\u2227\u00acC\u2261\u00acC\u2227(A\u2228C).\n$$",
